  "answerable": false,
  "question": "How well does AgentSSL perform on text classification tasks?",
  "status": "answered",
  "answer": "AgentSSL demonstrates strong performance in text classification tasks, exceeding the strongest human-engineered baselines in 8 out of 12 settings by up to +21.8% under weak feedback conditions and matched compute resources [agentssl-2611.17323v1:p1:para350:3]. However, it faces challenges with program selection, where performance can drop by as much as 47% when based on the agent’s feedback metric [agentssl-2611.17323v1:p1:para350:4]. The effectiveness of program selection is critical, as misalignment between the feedback metric and test performance can lead to substantial degradation in results [agentssl-2611.17323v1:p7:para350:3].",
